.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.cache

# WiFi credentials — machine-specific, never commit
include/wifi_config.h

# Claude Code — configuración local (rutas de máquina, permisos locales)
.claude/

# Junction local a incunest_afe4490 (no trackear — es un enlace de máquina)
lib/incunest_afe4490/

# Autogenerado por herramientas de build
compile_commands.json

# Logs de depuración (faulthandler, heartbeat, etc.)
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Archivos temporales / a eliminar
src/AFE44x0.c.to_delete

# Datos generados por ppg_plotter.py
ppg_data_snap_*.csv
ppg_data_stream_*.csv
# Capturas: los CSV no se versionan (pesan y son datos de sesión), pero SÍ la spec del set.
# Nota: hay que excluir el CONTENIDO (captures/*), no el directorio — git no permite reincluir
# ficheros dentro de un directorio excluido.
captures/*
!captures/CAPTURE_SET_SPEC.md
# truth.csv is AUTHORED (tier, ground truth, notes) — hand-written, small, and the only
# part of the capture set that cannot be regenerated. It must be versioned.
# Safe to commit only because capture filenames are coded (SUBJnn), never names: its
# 'file' column would otherwise publish the whole subject list in a single place.
!captures/truth.csv
# index.csv is DERIVED from the capture headers by tools/build_capture_index.py.
# Deliberately NOT versioned: it is a cache, and committing it would create a second
# source of truth for data that already lives in each capture's '#' header.
#
# SUBJECT_CODES.txt maps SUBJnn back to a person. It has NO exception here and must never
# get one — it is the one file that would undo the anonymisation of everything else.
#
# Capture data: no capture of a HUMAN SUBJECT is ever committed, coded name or not — it is
# health data. Simulator (MS100) captures contain nobody's data and MAY be committed one by
# one, with an explicit exception below, when a regression test depends on them: a test
# whose inputs live on a single machine is not reproducible. Nothing enters by accident.
#   e.g.  !captures/T1_SIM_STEADY_60BPM_96SPO2_20260905_101500.csv
#
# Analysis CODE of a campaign (captures/sessions/<campaign>_ANALYSIS/*.py) IS versioned: it is the
# method behind a number in the log (the HOSPNAV SpO2 bias, the R-method comparison) and holds no
# data -- it reads the CSVs beside it, which stay ignored, and names subjects only by their SUBJnn
# code. Git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so the chain below un-excludes
# the directories level by level and re-excludes their contents, letting only *.py through.
!captures/sessions/
captures/sessions/*
!captures/sessions/*_ANALYSIS/
captures/sessions/*_ANALYSIS/*
!captures/sessions/*_ANALYSIS/*.py

# Offline runner — build y ficheros generados
tools/offline_runner/build/
tools/offline_runner/*_result.csv
tools/offline_runner/batch_summary.csv
# Estado de la UI del script (geometrías de ventanas, celdas resaltadas) — por máquina
pulsenest_lab.ini

# Salidas de experimentos en la raíz (mover a captures/ si el resultado vale)
tia_linearity_sweep_*.csv
tia_linearity_sweep_*.png

# Documentación de terceros — NO redistribuir en un repo público.
# Ver docs/third_party_references.md para saber de dónde obtener cada documento.
docs/masimo_whitepapers/
docs/slaa655.pdf
docs/ISO_80601-2-61-2026.pdf
# WHO-UNICEF oxygen therapy device specifications (2019). CC BY-NC-SA, freely downloadable
# from WHO IRIS — kept out of the repo because linking is enough (see third_party_references.md).
docs/19061_WHO-UNICEF*.pdf

# ESP-IDF build: generated per-board build dirs and sdkconfig (scripts/build.ps1)
build/
build_V1[5-8]/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
managed_components/
test_lib/runner/build/

# Faulthandler log of the PPG viewer (per machine, like faulthandler.log)
tools/fleet_ppg_viewer_faulthandler.log
tools/fleet_ppg_viewer.ini
tools/pulsenest_recorder_gui.ini
tools/pulsenest_recorder_gui_faulthandler.log
